# OS
.DS_Store

# Old local history from before this went on github (safe to delete once you're happy)
.git-backup-pre-github/

# public server website lives here, kept out of the private mod repo (its own repo/deploy)
website/

# not part of the mod source
/dist/
/err.txt
/docs/
# tools/ is local scratch except for the pack publisher, which is real
# infrastructure: it holds the live version map, the CurseForge project ids and the
# config exclusion list, so it needs history. Note the contents have to be ignored
# with /tools/* rather than /tools/, because git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is itself excluded.
/tools/*
!/tools/publish-pack.py
# slice-web-ui.py regenerates the website's UI art FROM the in-game textures, so the site
# and the game cannot drift apart. Same reasoning as the publisher: it is the definition of
# a build step, not scratch, and it needs history.
!/tools/slice-web-ui.py
# rank-badges-rebuild.py is the ONLY way to add or change a rank badge: it trims the commissioned art,
# assigns each rank its codepoint by list position, and regenerates rank_index.json plus both font
# providers. Losing it would not just cost a script, it would strand the badge set exactly the way the
# Kakarot converter's mapping.json was stranded: the outputs survive and become unmaintainable. It holds
# no credentials, only the rank table and paths to local art.
!/tools/rank-badges-rebuild.py
# visualtest.sh is the entry point to the dev-only visual test harness (docs/visual-test-harness.md).
# It is real, versioned tooling like the scripts above, not scratch, so it is tracked.
!/tools/visualtest.sh
# check-eventbus-modids.py is a build guard for the core-plus-modules split: it fails the build if any
# @Mod.EventBusSubscriber lacks the correct explicit modid, or if a module presence check is hardcoded
# outside ModulePresence. common.gradle wires it into every project's `check`, so it is real build
# infrastructure and must be in history, not scratch.
!/tools/check-eventbus-modids.py
# check-client-key-reads.py is a build guard for the "private UI is not rendered without the key" rule: it
# fails the build if client-scoped code reads a server-side key/tier gate (RagnarokKey, KeyGate.unlocked/present,
# PublicContent, ...) instead of ClientGate. Wired into every project's `check`, so it is real
# build infrastructure and must be in history, not scratch.
!/tools/check-client-key-reads.py
# tools/parity is the 2.0 parity harness (run/diff scripts, guardrail allow-list, committed baselines): real
# infrastructure that needs history, not scratch. Re-include the directory so its contents are tracked; the
# per-run _server.log stays ignored via the pattern added near the run-dir rules above.
!/tools/parity/
# tools/s-phase holds the S-phase proof scripts (save-hash.sh, proof P6): real tooling, tracked.
!/tools/s-phase/
# tools/events-tests is the standalone event-model test harness (schedule math + byte-identical NBT codec).
# It compiles the shipped event sources against the mapped Minecraft jar and runs on plain Java, no Gradle.
# Real infrastructure that needs history, so re-include the directory.
!/tools/events-tests/
/staff-forums/
shuruisutilities/PORT_NOTES.md
shuruisutilities/TESTING_GUIDE.md
shuruisutilities/REWORK-GUI-PROMPT.txt
shuruis_raid_bosses/REWORK-GUI-PROMPT.txt
shuruis_raid_bosses/RESOURCEPACK-STRUCTURE-PROMPT.txt
shuruis_raid_bosses/RAID-CONFIGS-raditz-and-great-ape-vegeta.md
sdu/CUSTOM_MODELS.md
sdu/DISCORD_WIKI.md
sdu/GUIDE.md

# Local working area: decompiled sources, extracted third-party assets, montages and one-off
# probes. 4,500 of these were DragonMineZ's own extracted files, which are not ours to carry and
# have nothing to do with the suite. Kept on disk, out of the repo.
scratchpad/

# Projects that no longer belong to this repository. Their working copies are still on disk, and
# without these rules a plain `git add -A` silently re-adds them, which is exactly what happened
# once and dragged patreon-link/.dev.vars (worker secrets) back in with it.
/patreon-link/
/wolfskey/
/poposkey/
/world-tools/
/shuruis_mod_blacklist/
/dmz_mohist_melee_fix/
run2/
.gradle-run2/

# Parity harness (tools/parity): isolated per-label dev-run dirs at the repo root, and the per-run server
# log written next to each baseline. The baseline dump .txt files themselves ARE committed.
run-parity-*/
tools/parity/baselines/**/_server.log

# Local working dumps: decompiled DMZ sources and world/log scratch. Regenerated on demand,
# 233 MB and 2 MB respectively, and nothing in the build reads them.
scratchpad_dmz/
scratchpad_amb/

# Agent launch-test run dirs (fat/modular matrix); never commit dev-run output.
/run-core/
/run-all/
/run-dungeons/
/run-raids/
/run-tournaments/
/run-existing/
